couchjs: link the shared SpiderMonkey library

Debian's couch-libmozjs185-dev names the shared library libmozjs185.so, so
-lmozjs185-1.0 picked the static libmozjs185-1.0.a and the link failed on
NSPR's symbols. Look for mozjs185 first, as CouchDB 2 does; couchjs then
uses libmozjs185.so.1.0.

--- a/couchjs/c_src/SConscript
+++ b/couchjs/c_src/SConscript
@@ -67,7 +67,11 @@
         Exit(1)
 
     ## check for SpiderMonkey library as libjs or libmozjs
-    if not conf.CheckLibWithHeader('mozjs185-1.0', jsapi, 'c', autoadd=1):
+    # The shared libmozjs185 first: Debian's -dev package names it
+    # libmozjs185.so, and -lmozjs185-1.0 finds only the static archive,
+    # which then misses the NSPR symbols.
+    if not conf.CheckLibWithHeader('mozjs185', jsapi, 'c', autoadd=1) and \
+            not conf.CheckLibWithHeader('mozjs185-1.0', jsapi, 'c', autoadd=1):
         if not conf.CheckLibWithHeader('mozjs', jsapi, 'c', autoadd=1):
             if not conf.CheckLibWithHeader('js', jsapi, 'c', autoadd=1):
                 print 'Could not find JS library.', \
